<!--
  aiRA sitemap. Hand-maintained: this project has no build step, so a page
  added to the site has to be added here too.

  IT CARRIES <loc> AND NOTHING ELSE, on purpose.
  - changefreq and priority are ignored outright by Google and have been for
    years; writing them is inventing data that no one reads.
  - lastmod is left out because nothing here can keep it honest. With no build
    step it would be hand-typed, and Google ignores lastmod it finds
    untrustworthy, so a set of dates that quietly rot is worth less than none.
    Add it the day a build step can stamp it from git.

  THE LIST IS THE PAGES' OWN CANONICALS, read out of each file rather than
  written twice, so the two cannot disagree. The homepage is the one entry
  without a canonical tag to read; give index.html one and this stops being a
  special case.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: /404, /style-guide, /index-v2 and /index-v3,
  all of which carry a noindex meta. /pricing was absent too while it was
  parked and CAME BACK on 3 Oct with the page; it is entry 20.
-->
